Every count carries the command that produced it. Source equivalence vs 79f11389b is four files under tools/arifi-sync and NOTHING under ggml, src, common, tests, include or cmake. Evidence: 61 files, MISSING none, each row carrying the sha256 of the ORIGINAL and of the shipped copy where the scrub changed it. The S-X8 licence UNRESOLVED is CLOSED with the author's own LICENSE and NOTICE, sha256 recorded.

The export branch is BUILT in a separate clone and reports its own breakage honestly: all 415 sha-pinned ledger rows were dead after the rewrite, and the BASE PIN was dead too - which does not fail the audit, it silently widens it from 675 commits to 11500. Re-keyed from filter-repo's own commit-map with prior keys preserved. Author e-mail residue 403 -> 0; PATH residue unchanged, because a mailmap cannot reach paths that live in commit messages and historical blobs - that needs --replace-text or --invert-paths, which nobody authorised.

Tree identity: only 7 files differ outside content, all under patches/; 589 differ in content, of which 583 are under patches/ and 6 are exactly the re-keyed ledgers. HQ's criterion was 'patches/ and nothing else' - it is not met, by those 6, and that is reported as the proposed fix with its receipt rather than as a silently completed step.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native) - release engineering for this fork; no upstream origin exists.
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - an evidence document; no code path is touched.
